`]}),e.jsx(m,{compact:!0,projectionLayout:!0,clamps:["qk-clip"]}),e.jsxs(r,{title:"Reading the QK-Clip widget",children:[e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The widget holds one synthetic attention pattern: a query scored against twelve keys, with fixed relative sizes in which the largest score leads clearly and the second largest is 0.55 times the largest. The slider scales the whole pattern, its largest logit on a logarithmic track from 1.5 to 300, and panel (a) shows the logits before the controls as outline bars and after them as solid bars. Its axis is fixed, linear between ",e.jsx(s,{math:"-1",display:!1})," and ",e.jsx(s,{math:"1",display:!1})," and logarithmic beyond, so from ",e.jsx(s,{math:"\\pm 1",display:!1})," outward each tick is ten times the one before it. A dashed line marks ",e.jsx(s,{math:"\\tau = 100",display:!1}),"."]}),e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["With QK-Clip off, the top probability is about 55% at the starting value of 3, and the other eleven keys share the rest. It passes 96% at a largest logit of 8 and is above 99% at 12, so this pattern saturates long before its logits reach the hundreds. With QK-Clip on and the largest raw logit, ",e.jsx(s,{math:"S_{\\max}",display:!1}),", above 100, the solid bars are the outline bars scaled by ",e.jsx(s,{math:"100/S_{\\max}",display:!1}),", so the largest stays at 100, while the outline bars keep growing. On the logarithmic axis, that scaling makes every solid bar shorter than its outline by the same length. The top probability stays at 100.0% and the entropy at 0.000 nats. In this pattern a logit of 100 still saturates the softmax: the largest score leads the second by 45, and ",e.jsx(s,{math:"e^{-45} \\approx 3 \\times 10^{-20}",display:!1}),". The cap stops the logit from growing further. It does not, by itself, give the head a spread-out distribution again."]})]})]}),e.jsx(h,{caption:"A raw max logit of 225, the worked example for formula (6), with QK-Clip on. Each solid bar is its outline bar times 100/225 = 4/9, so the largest logit drops to 100 and the second to 55. The top probability still reads 100.0% and the entropy 0.000 nats, because a lead of 45 over the second key is enough to saturate the softmax.",children:e.jsx(m,{compact:!0,projectionLayout:!0,clamps:["qk-clip"],initialMaxLogit:225,initialActiveClamps:["qk-clip"]})}),e.jsxs(i,{title:"Stability comes from the whole training system",reading:!0,accent:2,number:"29",items:"5",children:[e.jsxs(t.ul,{children:[`
