`]}),e.jsxs(r,{title:"Why the first steps need a small learning rate",children:[e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Two conditions make the first steps of training fragile. Adam divides each coordinate's step by the square root of its second-moment estimate ",e.jsx(s,{math:"\\hat v_t",display:!1}),", and at the start ",e.jsx(s,{math:"\\hat v_t",display:!1})," is built from a handful of gradients, so the preconditioner rests on an immature, noisy statistic. The curvature of the loss is also high near initialization, so a full-size step can overshoot, and it does so in the worst part of the loss landscape. Warmup ramps the learning rate up from near zero, which keeps the early steps small while the optimizer state becomes meaningful. The course's schedule ramps it linearly over its warmup steps."]}),e.jsxs(t.table,{children:[e.jsx(t.thead,{children:e.jsxs(t.tr,{children:[e.jsx(t.th,{children:"Run"}),e.jsx(t.th,{children:"Warmup"})]})}),e.jsxs(t.tbody,{children:[e.jsxs(t.tr,{children:[e.jsx(t.td,{children:"Kimi K2"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"500 steps"})]}),e.jsxs(t.tr,{children:[e.jsx(t.td,{children:"DeepSeek V3"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"2,000 steps"})]}),e.jsxs(t.tr,{children:[e.jsx(t.td,{children:"OLMo 2"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"2,000 steps"})]}),e.jsxs(t.tr,{children:[e.jsx(t.td,{children:"MAI-Thinking-1"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"~12B tokens"})]})]})]}),e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The table shows how four labs size their warmup. Kimi K2 warms up for 500 steps ",e.jsx(a,{id:"kimik2-2025",children:"Kimi Team, 2025"}),", DeepSeek V3 for 2,000 steps ",e.jsx(a,{id:"deepseekv3-2024",children:"DeepSeek-AI, 2024b"}),", OLMo 2 for 2,000 steps ",e.jsx(a,{id:"olmo2-2025",children:"OLMo Team, 2025"}),", and MAI-Thinking-1 for about 12B tokens ",e.jsx(a,{id:"microsoftai2026maithinking1",children:"Microsoft AI Team, 2026"}),". The units differ: three runs report steps and one reports tokens. A step count converts to tokens only through the global batch size, and the batch size can itself change during a run."]})]})]}),e.jsxs(i,{title:"Cosine and multi-step schedules spend the budget differently",reading:!0,accent:3,number:"31",items:"4",children:[e.jsxs(t.ul,{children:[`
`,e.jsx(t.li,{children:"Cosine: decay to 10% of peak"}),`
