`,e.jsx(t.li,{children:"Then loss and pre-clip norm together"}),`
`]}),e.jsxs(r,{title:"One reading order for a run's dashboard",children:[e.jsx(t.p,{children:"Read a run's dashboard in a fixed order instead of scanning for the most dramatic curve. First align every trace and event log on optimizer-step IDs, and mark the earliest deviation in any trace, not merely the largest. Then go through the run in this order:"}),e.jsxs(t.ol,{children:[`
`,e.jsxs(t.li,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Schedule."})," Check the logged learning rate and phase first: warmup, stable or decay. A skipped warmup or a misplaced decay is visible at once. Compare the logged values with the intended schedule and with the state stored in the checkpoint, including the global batch size and the data-mixture phase."]}),`
