`]}),e.jsxs(r,{title:"Proxy models expose instabilities before a run scales up",children:[e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Wortsman et al. showed that two instabilities of large runs, attention-logit growth and output-logit divergence, also appear in small models trained at high learning rates ",e.jsx(a,{id:"wortsman2023smallscale",children:"Wortsman et al., 2024"}),". Qwen3.8-Flash-Next uses that proxy to test a recipe before scaling it. It holds a mixture-of-experts model with 25B total and 3B active parameters at a constant 2× or 4× its optimal learning rate, without the usual decay. It counts loss spikes, the steps whose loss lies more than 0.1 above a 201-step rolling median. It also tracks the 99.9th percentile of the pre-clip gradient norm, how often the norm crosses the clip threshold of 0.5, and each block's largest activation ",e.jsx(a,{id:"qwen2026qwen38flashnext",children:"Qwen Team, 2026"}),". At 4×, AdamW on the previous Qwen3.5 structure spiked 183 times per 10,000 steps, while Muon on the same structure never crossed the clip threshold in either of its two runs. In a pair of runs at 3× that differ only in a gated norm, a learned gate on the RMSNorm output, AdamW spiked 32.0 times per 10,000 steps without the gate and 3.2 times with it ",e.jsx(a,{id:"qwen2026qwen38flashnext",children:"Qwen Team, 2026"}),"."]}),e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Kolibri compared logit controls at its baseline learning rates, on a proxy with 7.8B total and 0.6B active parameters and grouped-query attention, one run per configuration over the first 53B tokens. With qk-norm, training stayed stable across the learning rates and batch sizes of its sweeps. Without qk-norm, the model diverged early and did not recover. A QK-Clip adapted to grouped-query attention, at ",e.jsx(s,{math:"\\tau = 100",display:!1})," in place of qk-norm, still showed gradient-norm spikes. Without qk-norm, training was stable at a tenth of the learning rate, and its loss then stayed above that of the model with qk-norm throughout the run ",e.jsx(a,{id:"alephalpha2026kolibri",children:"Aleph Alpha, 2026"}),". Your hot pair is a small test of the same kind."]})]})]}),e.jsxs(i,{title:"Norm placement and training hygiene are stability levers",reading:!0,accent:7,number:"48",children:[e.jsx(s,{math:"h = x + \\mathrm{RMSNorm}(\\mathrm{Attn}(x)) \\qquad h_{\\mathrm{out}} = h + \\mathrm{RMSNorm}(\\mathrm{MLP}(h))",label:"(11)"}),e.jsxs(t.ul,{children:[`
